{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass.</b> A second time, corresponding to the redemption from Egypt. And behold, this is a sign that he speaks of the days of the Messiah, for the redemption of the Second Temple was not a complete redemption, for all the tribes, even all of Judah, did not return to their land — and the one who interprets it of Hezekiah, that they gathered to his kingdom when they saw that Jerusalem was delivered and Sennacherib died after the death of most of his camp."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The note צ״ל רוב in brackets is a scribal correction: the manuscript reads רובי but should read רוב ('most of'). I translated according to the corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:25.634501876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}